+\subsection{Matched phensim benchmark with reference LDAK-KVIK}
+\label{sec:kvik-design}
+
+We froze a factorial protocol before examining association outcomes and
+used an excluded pilot to check interoperability and resource demands.
+Each cell has six independent genotype and phenotype replicates,
+$n=800$ diploid samples, and $m=6{,}000$ markers on six equal chromosomes.
+All genotypes and phenotypes are generated by phensim. Its
+\code{simulate\_population\_structure} function uses three populations
+with uniformly sampled membership and Balding--Nichols frequency drift.
+The software's \code{fst} parameter is zero or 0.05; it controls frequency
+dispersion and is not an empirical estimate of $F_{ST}$.
+Shared ancestral frequencies are $0.3+N(0,0.05^2)$, clipped to
+$[0.05,0.95]$; population frequencies are clipped to $[0.01,0.99]$.
+
+Two LD settings isolate local linkage from ancestry correlation.
+Markers are either independent conditional on population or generated
+in 50-marker blocks using two latent Gaussian AR(1) haplotypes per person
+with correlation parameter 0.8. Population-specific thresholds convert
+each haplotype to allele indicators. Blocks are independent conditional
+on population, but pooled genotypes share ancestry correlations across
+blocks and chromosomes. We added the optional block generator within
+phensim, preserving its existing independent-marker seeded draws.
+This controlled LD experiment does not reconstruct human demographic
+history. Markers with pooled minor-allele frequency below 0.01 are removed
+before either program receives them; calls are complete.
+
+The base global-null trait has no genetic effects and Gaussian residuals.
+The mixed trait has target genetic variance 0.5, divided equally between
+an infinitesimal background and ten normally distributed QTL effects.
+Both components use chromosomes 1--5 only, with QTLs in distinct blocks;
+chromosome 6 has no generating effects. Shared effects across populations
+are assumed. Phensim records every component, causal index and effect.
+For environmental confounding we pass population labels $-1,0,1$ as an
+explicit exposure $E$, standardized within the sample, and form
+\begin{equation}
+ y=\operatorname{standardize}\left\{\sqrt{s}E+
+       \sqrt{1-s}(u+q+e)\right\},\qquad s\in\{0,0.2\}.
+ \label{eq:phensim-environment}
+\end{equation}
+The component targets are not asserted to equal realized variance
+fractions: population structure can correlate $E$, $u$ and $q$.
+The archive therefore includes their covariance matrix.
+
+Four analysis cells comprise unstructured data, structured data without
+environmental effects, structured data with the exposure, and the same
+confounded phenotype adjusted for the two leading genotype PCs. PCs are
+computed without phenotypes and supplied identically to all methods.
+Every analysis includes an intercept. Exact LOCO EMMAX, local BOLT-inf,
+local KVIK and reference LDAK-KVIK use their default fitting and
+calibration settings with explicit seeds and one thread. These are
+comparisons of supplied procedures, whose priors and tuning searches
+differ; matching inputs does not make their statistical models identical.
+
+Phensim writes PLINK calls counting BIM allele A2. An independent decoder
+checks every BED call against the simulated matrix; mixmogam must read
+the complementary A1 counts. LDAK's own statistics command verifies the
+same marker IDs, sample IDs, allele labels, allele means and call rates.
+Both analysis programs read the same BED/BIM/FAM files and serialized
+phenotypes and covariates. The official native Mac executable
+\code{ldak6.3.mac} is pinned to repository revision \code{995e18753a0a},
+with its full URL and SHA256 in the archive; the generic ``Version 6''
+banner alone does not identify this build.
+
+Calibration is measured on all markers under the global genetic null,
+and separately on chromosome 6 under the mixed trait. The latter shares
+ancestry with causal chromosomes, so rejection assesses control of
+ancestry associations as well as statistical approximation. Other markers
+are not automatically labelled null simply because they are not large
+QTLs. We report rejection at 0.05, 0.01 and 0.001, genomic inflation from
+p-equivalent chi-square statistics, and population-loading, frequency and
+local-LD quintiles. Loading is the fraction of genotype sum of squares
+explained by population membership, chosen without phenotype outcomes.
+Power is direct causal-marker detection at $0.05/m$ and $5\times10^{-8}$.
+Monte Carlo standard errors use independent replicate panels, not the
+number of correlated markers. Six replicates cannot establish calibration
+at genome-wide significance thresholds.
+
+Each method runs in a separate process. Wall time includes startup, input
+loading, fitting, scanning and result writing; reference time sums its
+two stages. Kernel \code{wait4} counters provide peak resident memory,
+using the larger stage peak for the reference. Common simulation,
+export validation and PC construction are recorded separately. Method
+order rotates across replicates, code caches may be warm, and the macOS
+power guard requires AC power with Low Power Mode disabled. This is a
+bounded laptop comparison, not a biobank-scale performance claim.
+
